<Base title="About | Niccolò Parlanti">
  <section class="page-heading wrap"><p class="eyebrow">ABOUT / NICCOLÒ PARLANTI</p><h1>Penetration tester.<br /><em>Bug bounty hunter.</em></h1><p class="lede">I test applications, investigate vulnerabilities, and manage security campaigns and triage at UNGUESS.</p></section>
  <section class="about-grid wrap"><aside class="mono">OFFENSIVE SECURITY<br />RESEARCH & PRACTICE</aside><div class="prose"><h2>What I do.</h2><p>I work as a penetration tester and hunt vulnerabilities through bug bounty programs. At UNGUESS, I manage triage and security testing campaigns for private organizations.</p><p>These roles inform each other. Testing means investigating how a system behaves under unexpected conditions. Triage means checking the evidence, understanding the context, and making the impact clear enough for someone else to act on it.</p><h2>Areas of work</h2><dl class="expertise"><dt>Penetration testing</dt><dd>Investigating application behavior, access controls, and the assumptions that connect components.</dd><dt>Vulnerability research</dt><dd>Following unusual behavior, developing reproducible evidence, and documenting the underlying cause.</dd><dt>Triage & campaign management</dt><dd>Assessing reports and coordinating security testing for private organizations through my work at UNGUESS.</dd></dl><h2>Background</h2><p>This site collects selected public advisories and technical writing. The older CTF and certification articles remain part of the archive: a record of the learning that led here.</p><p>My academic background includes the University of Florence and the EIT Digital Master School, with studies at the University of Trento and the University of Twente.</p><p>Outside security, I spend time in the mountains and travel when I can.</p></div></section>
  <section class="contact-band wrap" id="contact"><p class="eyebrow">CONTACT</p><h2>Work <em>with me.</em></h2><p>For freelance penetration testing, send me a brief description of your project and preferred timeframe. Research collaborations are welcome too.</p><a class="contact-email" href="mailto:parlanti.niccolo@gmail.com">parlanti.niccolo@gmail.com ↗</a><div class="hero-actions"><a class="text-link" href="/#freelance">Freelance pentesting ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/Niccolo10">GitHub ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/niccol%C3%B2-parlanti/">LinkedIn ↗</a></div></section>
